bcom:source-76700ab8654d62de4e09069bcabfec7c86303a8d78ddd1fd55fdb3bed0bc415d bco:citesClaim "1"^^xsd:integer .
bcom:source-76700ab8654d62de4e09069bcabfec7c86303a8d78ddd1fd55fdb3bed0bc415d bco:citesSource bcos:SRC-GOV-04 .
bcom:source-76700ab8654d62de4e09069bcabfec7c86303a8d78ddd1fd55fdb3bed0bc415d bco:departureNote "NAF's C1 view organizes capabilities into specialization and aggregation taxonomies, independent of implementation. A BCO Capability Map is not a taxonomy of capability types: it describes one organization, its entries are Capability Assessments and Capability Targets, and the arrangement of entries asserts no parthood or specialization among capabilities (CD14, CD17). What a capability type means is stated once, in its class definition and catalog concept."@en .
bcom:source-76700ab8654d62de4e09069bcabfec7c86303a8d78ddd1fd55fdb3bed0bc415d bco:locator "NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide, section 5, C1 Capability Taxonomy, p.17" .
